{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וכל הנשים", :translit "v'khol ha-nashim", :gloss "and all the women"} {:he "וכל הנשים יתנו יקר", :translit "v'khol ha-nashim yit'nu y'kar", :gloss "and all the women shall give splendor"} {:he "וכל הנשים העומדות", :translit "v'khol ha-nashim ha-omdot", :gloss "and all the women who stood"} {:he "יתנו יקר", :translit "yit'nu y'kar", :gloss "they shall give splendor"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["וכל הנשים" "וכל הנשים יתנו יקר" "וכל הנשים העומדות"]}], :frame {:text "Jeremiah rebuked the people, and specifically the queens and women, for burning incense to the host of the heavens — the sun, moon, and stars — in violation of God's command, and warned that this idolatry would lead to exile and their becoming a byword and taunt among the nations (Jeremiah 44). Exodus 35:26 describes righteous women who spun goat hair for the Tabernacle; Jeremiah 13:18 addresses the queen and women with 'וכל הנשים העומדות'; and the phrase 'יתנו יקר' in Proverbs 31:10 describes the valor and splendor a woman of excellence bestows.", :sources ["Jeremiah 44:15-19" "Jeremiah 44:8" "Exodus 35:26" "Jeremiah 13:18" "Proverbs 31:10"]}} {:quotes [{:he "אותנה", :translit "otanah", :gloss "them (feminine)"} {:he "עד אשר הפיצותם אותנה", :translit "ad asher h'fitztem otanah", :gloss "until you scattered them"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["אותנה" "עד אשר הפיצותם אותנה"]}], :frame {:text "Ezekiel 34 rebukes the shepherds of Israel who fed themselves instead of the flock and trampled the pasture with their feet, scattering the sheep; God promises to gather them and set over them one shepherd, His servant David (Ezekiel 34:2-23). In Exodus 35:26 the same feminine pronoun 'אותנה' appears in the context of the righteous women building the Tabernacle, a cause for the Shechinah's presence among Israel; in Ezekiel it appears in the context of shepherds who fail the flock, driving the Shechinah away.", 